<title>USA: Motorola gets GSM contract in India.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets GSM contract in India.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola's International Cellular Infrastructure Division said Thursday it received a contract to install a Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM) wireless phone network in India.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed, but Motorola said the contract brings the total value of contracts awarded to Motorola ICID in India to $300 million.</p>
<p>The contract is with the Reliance Group of Industries, in alliance with NYNEX Corp, Motorola said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
